<title>SOUTH AFRICA: London Clubs Int eyes SAfrica casino - report.</title>
<headline>London Clubs Int eyes SAfrica casino - report.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British-based London Clubs International Plc (LCI) was reported on Sunday to be leading a bid to build a 1.7 billion rand casino and leisure centre in South Africa's commercial capital Johannesburg.</p>
<p>The South African Sunday Times said the &quot;Rivers of Gold&quot; development, planned on a 20-hectare site in the centre of the city, could create 12,000 jobs.</p>
<p>The paper said LCI would take a 20 percent stake in the project, which depended on a casino licence being granted.</p>
<p>((-- Cape Town newsroom +2721 252238))</p>
